WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.881 line:78%
Jira says what to build.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.545 line:78%
GitHub, what to review.

3
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.435 line:78%
Your agent lives in a terminal.

4
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.021 line:78%
And nothing connects them.

5
00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:11.902 line:78%
Orynx brings it together. Hand your agent the ticket, and keep your flow.

6
00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.536 line:78%
Your sprint, and your own tickets, side by side.

7
00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.788 line:78%
Anything is one keystroke away.

8
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.729 line:78%
Paste a ticket key, and send it to Claude.

9
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:28.042 line:78%
It works in its own git worktree, so your checkout stays untouched.

10
00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.903 line:78%
What it did reads like a checklist, not a wall of chat.

11
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.910 line:78%
The raw output stays in the terminal, where it belongs.

12
00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:38.775 line:78%
Anything risky waits for your click.

13
00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.692 line:78%
Or go hands-off. You decide how far it goes.

14
00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:46.053 line:78%
Even from your phone.

15
00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:50.484 line:78%
Then it ships the pull request.

16
00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:56.795 line:78%
Orynx. It runs on your machine, and your tokens stay in your keychain.
